The bug is caused by not releasing the reference to the device node (`comp->dev_node`) in the error paths of the `mtk_mdp_comp_init` function. When an error occurs, the function would return without calling `of_node_put(comp->dev_node);`, leading to a memory leak due to the unbalanced reference counting.



